From: Alan Shearer
Subject: mouse: keep the watcher alive on B_DEVICE_NOT_READY

USB HID checksum and transfer errors come back as Device not ready.
The regular mouse path exits the control thread on any error other
than B_INTERRUPTED. The mouse stays dead until the device is unplugged
or the machine reboots.

Snooze a bit and try the read again. Same idea as the touchpad path
already does for timeouts and bad data.

---
src/add-ons/input_server/devices/mouse/MouseInputDevice.cpp | 6 ++++++
1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/input_server/devices/mouse/MouseInputDevice.cpp b/src/add-ons/input_server/devices/mouse/MouseInputDevice.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/input_server/devices/mouse/MouseInputDevice.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/input_server/devices/mouse/MouseInputDevice.cpp
@@ -406,6 +406,12 @@
 			if (ioctl(fDevice, MS_READ, &movements, sizeof(movements)) != B_OK) {
 				if (errno == B_INTERRUPTED)
 					continue;
 
+				// USB checksum / transfer errors show up as device not ready.
+				// Do not kill the watcher for that.
+				if (errno == B_DEVICE_NOT_READY) {
+					snooze(10000);
+					continue;
+				}
+
 				LOG_ERROR("Mouse device exiting, %s\n", strerror(errno));
 				_ControlThreadCleanup();
 				// TOAST!
 				return;
 			}
